t wasted draws now carry a real cost"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Turn 3, unlimited passes"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"~79%"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"~15â€“25%"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Stock alignment puzzle, softened by endless recycling"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Turn 3, three passes"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Below ~79%"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"~10â€“20%"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"The traditional hard game; every pass must be planned"}]]}]]}]]}]}]
4:["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Two things are worth noticing. First, the theoretical numbers barely move between Turn 1 and Turn 3 â€” only about three points â€” because a perfect player can eventually reach almost any stock card by manipulating the waste. Second, the realistic numbers move enormously, because human players cannot track alignment perfectly. Turn 3 does not make deals much less winnable; it makes winning lines much harder to find. That distinction is the single most useful fact on this page."}]
5:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-10 space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"How often is a deal unplayable from the start?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"A deal is \"unplayable\" when not a single move exists at the opening position â€” no tableau card can move onto another, no Ace is exposed, and nothing useful ever surfaces from the stock. These true dead deals are rarer than frustrated players assume. Simulation studies put the figure at roughly 0.025% under Turn 1 rules â€” about one deal in 4,000 â€” and around 0.25%, one in 400, under Turn 3, where two-thirds of the stock is harder to reach."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"So when an opening looks hopeless, it almost never is. What players usually experience as an unplayable game is actually an early deadlock: a few legal moves existed, but they led into a blocked position within the first dozen plays. Those early losses count against the winnable percentage above, but they are a different animal from a deal with no legal move at all â€” and with undo available, many of them are recoverable by backing up and choosing a different line."}]]}]
6:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-10 space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"What Easy, Medium, and Hard mean for your odds here"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"This app's three difficulty settings map directly onto the rule sets in the table above â€” the shuffle itself is always fair and random, so difficulty changes how much the rules forgive, never which cards you get."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border bg-[hsl(var(--card))] shadow-sm","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"Setting"}],["$","th",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"Draw"}],["$","th",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"Stock passes"}],["$","th",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"What it does to your odds"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Easy"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Turn 1"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Unlimited"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"The best odds Klondike offers â€” ideal for warm-ups and win streaks"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Medium"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Turn 1"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"3"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Full stock visibility, but each of the three passes must produce progress"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Hard"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Turn 3"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"3"}],["$","td",null,{"className":"border-b px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"The classic tough ruleset â€” expect win rates in the teens and treat 20% as elite"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"A practical suggestion for daily players: track your statistics on one setting at a time. A win percentage only means something against a fixed ruleset, and moving between Easy and Hard mid-week makes your numbers unreadable. Many regulars keep Easy for casual sessions and log their \"real\" record on Medium or Hard."}]]}]
7:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-10 space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"Odds trivia worth knowing"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"A few smaller probabilities shape how a session feels. Only seven of the 52 cards are face up when the tableau is dealt, and straightforward combinatorics says at least one of the four Aces is among them roughly 45% of the time. That is why some deals feel fast out of the gate â€” an exposed Ace goes straight to the foundations and immediately flips a fresh card â€” while the other 55% of games open with excavation work before the first foundation card appears. Neither opening predicts the outcome; plenty of ace-up deals collapse and plenty of slow starts cascade home."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Streak math matters for morale, too. At a healthy 30% win rate, the chance of losing any particular run of five games is about 17% â€” so a five-game losing streak is not a slump, it is a Tuesday. Even at an expert-level 43%, you will lose four straight about once in every ten four-game stretches. Daily players who know these numbers stop reading meaning into cold runs and keep their decisions steady, which is itself worth a few percentage points over a season of play."}]]}]
8:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-10 space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"Closing the gap: playing closer to the ceiling"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":["You cannot see through face-down cards, but you can stop donating winnable games. The biggest leaks are the same for almost everyone: rushing cards to the foundations before they finish their tableau work, flipping fewer face-down cards than an alternative line would have, emptying columns without a King ready, and drawing through the stock without a plan in a limited-pass game. The"," ",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"1eb72b087b11889a850b.htc","className":"font-semibold text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline","children":"strategy guide"}]," ","covers each of these in detail, and the"," ",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/turn-3","className":"font-semibold text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline","children":"Turn 3 page"}]," ","digs into stock-alignment tactics specific to the draw-three game."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"One more encouraging number to leave with: since roughly 79% of deals are winnable and strong players convert around 43% on Turn 1, the average player's realistic upside is not a few points â€” it is often double their current rate. In Klondike, unlike most games of chance, the odds genuinely reward the time you put in."}]]}]
9:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-10 rounded-lg border bg-[hsl(var(--card))] p-6 shadow-sm","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))]","children":"Test the odds yourself"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 leading-8 text-[hsl(var(--content-fg-muted))]","children":"Pick a difficulty, play a fresh deal, and let the built-in statistics keep score. Four out of five deals can be beaten â€” the interesting question is how many you can find."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/#game","className":"inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-primary-foreground hover:opacity-90","children":"Play Klondike Solitaire"}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"1eb72b087b11889a850b.htc","className":"inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-lg border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))] hover:bg-[hsl(var(--muted))]","children":"Solitaire Strategy"}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/turn-3","className":"inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-lg border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-[hsl(var(--content-fg))] hover:bg-[hsl(var(--muted))]","children":"Turn 3 Solitaire"}]]}]]}]
